%description:

Tcp.receiveBufferLowRtt:above-rtt -- the receive buffer grows in proportion to the RTT.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "windowAutoTuning: below this receive RTT, Dynamic Right-Sizing grows the
receive buffer in proportion to the RTT; above it, the buffer may double each RTT, as for slow
start".

The classes: below-rtt (1 ms, the default, the value of Linux, below the receive RTT) and
above-rtt (a value above the receive RTT). The code: TcpConnection::growRcvBuffer(), at each
read after one receive RTT (Dynamic Right-Sizing), grows the window by the window times the
receive RTT over the value when the RTT is below the value, else by twice the window times the
relative growth of the bytes read. This test separates "above-rtt" from "below-rtt".

Host under test: host2, with window auto-tuning and a receive buffer of 131072 bytes
(preconditions), whose application reads at once; host1 sends 20000000 bytes; the round trip
is 40 ms. Observation: level 3, at 0.7 s, the receive buffer of host2 is at most 600000 bytes (about
440000); 100 ms gives about 900000, in proportion to the RTT.

%# parameter: Tcp.receiveBufferLowRtt
%# class: above-rtt
%# value: 1s
%# key: *.host2.tcp.receiveBufferLowRtt
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpReceiveBufferLowRttAboveRtt")
        .act(action().at(0.7)
                 .describe("the receive buffer of host2 at 0.7 s")
                 .assertModule("host2.tcp.conn-*", "state.rcvBufferSize <= 600000"));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpReceiveBufferLowRttAboveRtt compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.receiveBufferLowRtt = 1s    # the parameter under test
*.host2.tcp.windowAutoTuning = true
*.host2.tcp.receiveBufferSize = 131072B
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 20000000B
sim-time-limit = 0.8s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpReceiveBufferLowRttAboveRtt: PASS
